An important observation is that if the original state $\x_0$ is known, it becomes easy to model the transition between $\x_t$ and $\x_{t-1}$, i.e. to infer and remove the added noise. The conditional distribution $q(\x_{t-1}|\x_t, \x_0)$ can be computed as follows:

