    &= \frac{q(\x_t|\x_{t-1})q(\x_{t-1}|\x_0)}{q(\x_t|\x_0)}&& \text{Markov property}\\
\end{align*}

Since $q(\x_t|\x_0)$ acts as a normalisation constant independent of $\x_{t-1}$, it can be omitted when considering the shape of the distribution. Thus, the following proportional relationship holds:
